    "lawCode": "Amd §605-a, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7580A\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to scholarships for\nacademic excellence\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to enable Scholarships for Academic Excel-\nlence to be fully utilized.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends subdivision 2 of section 605-a of the education law to\nprovide that if an award is declined by a student prior to the end of\ntheir high school program, the scholarship shall be awarded, to the\nextent practicable, to the next most qualified student.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThe amendment modifies the effective date and provisions related to\nawarding the scholarship to the next most qualified student.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law provides for 8,000 Scholarships for Academic Excellence\nannually. The top scholar of each public or private high school in the\nstate is eligible for a scholarship and the remaining balance of the\nawards are distributed to students using a weighted average of scores\nfrom certain Regents examinations. Unfortunately, if a student declines\nthe scholarship or such scholarship is revoked, the scholarship goes\nunused. This legislation would award the scholarship to the next most\nqualified student in the event that a student declines an award.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-24: Referred to the Committee on Higher Education\n\n2021-22: A06827; Referred to the Committee on Higher Education\n\n2019-20: A2958; Referred to the Committee on Higher Education\n\n2017-18: A3634; Referred to the Committee on Higher Education\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect July 1, 2026.\n",
